instrumentalist. born July 8, 1970, in Los Angeles, California, USA. Son of [a=David Campbell] and [a=Bibbe Hansen], grandson of [a=Al Hansen]. He was married to [a=Marissa Ribisi] from 2004–2019.\r\n\r\nWhen his parents split, he and his younger brother stayed with their mother. Beck dropped out of school at the age of 14 and drifted around for about a decade, ending up back in Los Angeles. While playing some open-mike events, he got noticed by the little local label Bong Load Custom Records. In 1993, \"Loser\" was released to the world in a limited pressing of 500 copies and sent out to radio DJs across the U.S. The song became quite popular, and subsequently DGC/Geffen/MCA signed Beck in November of 1993, while giving him the freedom to work with independent labels and to make uncommercial music. The DGC release of Loser in January 1994 became an international hit.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:3928","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":104321,"name":"Beck Hansen"},{"id":2426988,"name":"Mollusk (2)"},{"id":3838081,"name":"Bek David Campbell"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Beck !","Beck Hansen","Beck!","貝克","벡 !"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/3928-Beck","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.beck.com/","https://www.facebook.com/Beck","https://twitter.com/beck","https://www.instagram.com/beck","https://vimeo.com/videotheque","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beck","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0065059/","https://www.youtube.com/@beck","https://www.youtube.com/@BeckVEVO","https://whiskeyclone.net/","https://soundcloud.com/planned_obsolescence"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/7577859/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"7577859","image":"","imageThumb":"","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:7577859","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/7577859-Leshutler","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs